// What a new game's compile may cost (ticket 2009, ADR-0049). CI's
// `compile-times` job runs `cargo xtask compile-times --budget` on this
// file (crates/xtask/src/compile_times.rs) and fails over it.
Budget(
    // The most the median rebuild of a new `grid` game may take after a
    // one-line change in its `main.rs`, in seconds, on CI's runner of each
    // OS (`std::env::consts::OS`): the slowest measured, plus 50 % for the
    // runners' noise. Linux measured 0.72 to 1.04 s, Windows (MSVC) 1.79
    // to 1.95 s. A slower rebuild is found and fixed, not budgeted.
    rebuild: {
        "linux": 0.0,
        "windows": 0.0,
    },
    // The most crates a new `blank` game's dependency tree may hold, the
    // engine's among them (`cargo metadata`, every platform's, with the
    // engine's Cargo.lock). A change that adds one raises this number in
    // the same PR, so each new dependency is a choice.
    dependencies: 143,
)
